@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
' '   description:  Hotel booking collaboration with nested numbering, a self-message, and conditional messages.
'   usecase:      Teach nested numbering (1.1, 1.2, 2), self-messages, and conditional messages.
'   complexity:   medium
'   domain:       travel
' ============================================================================
title Example Communication - Medium Booking Collaboration

actor "Guest" as Guest
participant "BookingUI" as BookingUI
participant "ReservationSvc" as ReservationSvc
participant "InventorySvc" as InventorySvc
participant "PaymentSvc" as PaymentSvc
participant "NotificationSvc" as NotificationSvc

' TOP-LEVEL messages (1, 2, 3...) are the major steps in order.
' NESTED messages (1.1, 1.2) are the sub-calls that make up step 1.

Guest --> BookingUI : 1: searchRooms(checkIn, checkOut)
BookingUI --> InventorySvc : 1.1: queryAvailability()
InventorySvc --> BookingUI : 1.2: returnAvailableRooms()
BookingUI --> Guest : 1.3: showResults()

Guest --> BookingUI : 2: selectRoom(roomId)
BookingUI --> ReservationSvc : 2.1: createHold(roomId)

' GUARDED / CONDITIONAL message: only fires if the bracketed condition holds.
' PlantUML has no dedicated conditional syntax on links, so we annotate it.
ReservationSvc --> PaymentSvc : 2.2: preAuthorizeCard()[card_on_file]

' SELF-MESSAGE: an object sends a message to itself along its own link.
' Useful for showing internal validation or state mutation.
ReservationSvc --> ReservationSvc : 2.3: setExpiryTimer()

Guest --> BookingUI : 3: confirmBooking()
BookingUI --> ReservationSvc : 3.1: confirm()
ReservationSvc --> PaymentSvc : 3.2: capturePayment()
ReservationSvc --> NotificationSvc : 3.3: sendConfirmation()
NotificationSvc --> Guest : 3.4: emailConfirmation()

' TEACHING NOTES:
'   - Nested numbering reveals CALL HIERARCHY: 1.1 and 1.2 both happen
'     while message 1 is being serviced.
'   - A self-message (2.3) does NOT leave the object; it shows internal work.
'   - Conditional messages (2.2) carry a guard — they may or may not fire.
'   - The same link can carry many numbered messages over time.
@enduml
